+## Benchmark scenes A–E, weather, time of day (stage scenes)
+
+The five scenes the Victus benchmark measures (D-078 QM8; the harness's default slots), each on the env temperate
+battlefield with its forest, river and Iron Age village. Scenes C and D are driven by a battle that the prototype
+TacticalResolver fought on this terrain grid (DR49 item 5); presentation reads the trace only (DR42). Details,
+captures, G1-vs-G2 sheets, llvmpipe costs and what still looks placeholder: `reports/scenes.md`; provenance:
+`assets/PROVENANCE.md` §3.13.
+
+| Scene | Slot | Content |
+|---|---|---|
+| `bench-a` | A | Soldier close-up: a hoplite with the painted aspis and his bare-headed commander with the hero aspis, three of the line and a standard, all in the authored hoplite guard (no CMU motion); the commander's expression runs grim → battle cry → calm |
+| `bench-b` | B | Formation: 320 instanced soldiers of both forces in four blocks with four standards and officers on the meadow by the village (the harness's crowd sweep sets the count) |
+| `bench-c` | C | Large battlefield: the 2,100 soldiers of the exported battle, each driven by the trace (positions, states, blows, falls, surrenders); the clash and melee shots look where the trace's blows fall thickest |
+| `bench-d-shown`, `bench-d-cutaway` | D | Cinematic aftermath from the trace's recorded outcome: field, prisoners, the surrender, faces, standards, smoke and dust; the last beat shows the fallen or cuts away. The death-content setting has **no default** (D-079 Q12 is open); slot D is bound to `bench-d-shown` as the measurement's upper bound only |
+| `bench-e` | E | Campaign environment: vistas of the forest, the river valley, the village and a stone stronghold (at noon, golden hour and dusk, and one higher view over the village to the stronghold), a river view, the settlement and the fortification (benchmark capture only; the campaign map is unchanged, D-079 Q7) |
