+scripts/export-battle-trace.sh [--check]   # the battle of scenes C and D: $G2_ASSETS/baked/trace/battle-2100.g2bt (+ MANIFEST.tsv)
+dotnet Gfx.Demo/bin/Release/net10.0/Gfx.Demo.dll --capture bench-c --out DIR --size 1920x1080 [--set weather=rain] [--shots a,b]
+dotnet Gfx.Demo/bin/Release/net10.0/Gfx.Demo.dll --bench bench-b --shot wide-noon --variants "g2;weather=rain;weather=mist"
+dotnet Gfx.Demo/bin/Release/net10.0/Gfx.Demo.dll --suite smoke            # the harness on slots A-E (the benchmark scenes)
+scripts/capture-scenes.sh OUT_DIR [GROUPS] [SAMPLES]   # the canonical 1920x1080 stills (G2_DEMO_DLL: run a copy of the build)
+scripts/bench-scenes.sh OUT_DIR                        # llvmpipe costs: smoke suite on the benchmark scenes and the G1 stand-ins, weather
+```
+
+- **Weather** (`--set`, presentation only, off by default: every term 0 renders the frame of the earlier stages):
+  `weather=clear|overcast|mist|rain`, or the terms `cloud`, `wet`, `rain`, `mist` (0..1). Cloud blends the sky towards
+  an overcast sky and dims the sun; wetness darkens porous surfaces and adds a water film (terrain, foliage, skin,
+  cloth, kit, structures); rain adds puddles on level ground and rain streaks; mist thickens a low height fog.
+- **Time of day:** the scenes' shots carry their hours (`BenchHours`: noon 12.5 h, golden hour 17.9 h, dusk 18.62 h);
+  B, C and E have one shot at each hour.
+- **Loading:** each scene loads the env battlefield (25–60 s in the canonical captures on llvmpipe here, 22–43 s of it
+  the tree impostor bake); C and D also need `scripts/export-battle-trace.sh` to have run, and A–D the chars, kit-outfit and crowd bakes.
