+outfits (§3.11), the crowd LOD3 bake and animation bank (§3.12), the env temperate battlefield with its forest, river
+and Iron Age village (§3.10) and the render1 terrain and sky (§3.8).
+
+| Output or runtime use | Inputs | Transformations | Licence of the output | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Battle trace of scenes C and D, `$G2_ASSETS/baked/trace/battle-2100.g2bt` (681,135 bytes, sha256 `35e7f65def34690ff7ecc1f30dca0366583ee627d5c09f0fca935d4ef8c65a7b`, trace content hash `7670DF68DAE2048430DC62E4DE2BDE2976B894EE0EA24CA5F9E30D848ADF331A`), `MANIFEST.tsv` | the battle prototype's TacticalResolver (`prototypes/m7-sprint1/Proto.M7`, project code, referenced read-only at tree `ce495ee6fd415f90ae880af7b93b655c822b1511`, never modified); the env temperate fixture grid (§3.10, generated from fixture inputs) and the env Iron Age village plan (generated) | `scripts/export-battle-trace.sh` → `tools/traceexport`: 21 heavy-infantry formations of 50 per side (2,100 entities) deployed on a 20 m battle grid downscaled from the 4 m fixture grid (5 × 5 cells per battle cell, the village as Building cells; a PROTOTYPE ADAPTER), the resolver stepped with its knowledge AI on both sides to the end of the battle, every 2 s snapshot (positions in mm, states) and every Fire and Damage event recorded, written as JSON and re-encoded by the presentation's reader into the compact binary form (gzip, zigzag varints; exact integers, same content hash). `--check` re-exports and compares the content hash. Never committed | project-generated data | own |
