+(§3.8: CC0, MIT and CC-BY-4.0 sets; notices §5).
+
+**Algorithms implemented from publications or common practice** (no code copied, no asset): wet surfaces darkening
+porous materials and smoothing every surface with a water film, rough surfaces keeping at least half their roughness
+(after Lagarde, "Water drop 2b – Dynamic rain and its effects", 2013), an overcast sky as a blend towards a uniform CIE
+overcast luminance distribution (Moon and Spencer 1942, the CIE standard overcast sky), exponential height fog for
+ground mist (common practice), camera-facing rain-streak quads in a wrapped box around the camera and camera-facing
+soft smoke billboards with a Henyey–Greenstein forward-scattering lobe, shaded as soft spheres and faded near the
+camera, the dust layer's opacity following its optical depth along the view (1/sin of the view elevation for a thin
+horizontal layer) (common practice; Henyey and Greenstein 1941).
